 # Voxel Ray Marching with Traversal Order Optimization
 
-Also called: 33 float points ray marching, 3D Texture Path Tracer, Volume Ray Marching
+Also called: 33 float points ray marching, 3D Texture Path Tracer
 
 ## Overview
-Voxel Ray Marching with Traversal Order Optimization renders a 3D voxel texture by marching rays from the camera through the volume, compositing samples with front-to-back alpha blending to visualize the volume [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard fixed-step ray marching by optimizing the traversal order of voxel boundaries using precomputed time deltas ($t_{\Delta}$) and maximum boundary times ($t_{max}$), minimizing floating-point operations per step [S2, unofficial]. The algorithm advances analytically from one cell boundary to the next, avoiding fixed-distance sampling steps [G].
+Voxel Ray Marching with Traversal Order Optimization renders a 3D voxel texture by advancing a ray from the camera to the back plane, compositing samples via front-to-back alpha blending to visualize the volume [S1, unofficial]. It differs from its parent [Ray Marching Optimization](10233-ray-marching-optimization.md) by specifically minimizing floating-point operations during traversal through precomputed step deltas and explicit axis-based boundary comparison [S2, unofficial]. It is distinct from [Tiled Ray Marching with Grid Sampling](2586-tiled-ray-marching-with-grid-sampling.md) by operating on a per-ray basis without tile-based batching, and from [Volume Ray Marching Optimization](14309-volume-ray-marching-optimization.md) by relying on fixed-step or grid-aligned traversal logic rather than adaptive step sizing based on density gradients [S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Inputs:**
-    *   Ray origin ($r_{origin}$) and direction ($r_{direction}$), normalized [S2, unofficial].
-    *   Voxel grid dimensions ($V_{grid} = (W, H, D)$) in number of voxels [S2, unofficial].
-    *   Physical volume size ($V_{size}$) [S2, unofficial].
-    *   3D texture sampler ($T_{3D}$) containing RGBA voxel data [S1, S2, unofficial].
-    *   Alpha clip threshold ($\alpha_{clip}$) [S2, unofficial].
-    *   (Optional) Front/Back FBO textures for ray origin determination [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Outputs:**
-    *   Computed color ($C_{out}$) and hit status [S1, S2, unofficial].
-
-**Data Structures:**
-*   `recordVolume`: A structure holding the ray hit result.
-    *   `hit` (bool): True if an opaque voxel was found.
-    *   `color` (vec3): The accumulated or hit color.
+This method builds on [Ray-grid traversal](17-ray-grid-traversal.md), which advances analytically from one cell boundary to the next. The core mechanism determines the next cell by comparing distances to upcoming boundaries on the x, y, and z axes, selecting the minimum distance to advance.
